# bnbagent-studio workspace defaults.
# All agent secrets — the encrypted keystore AND .env.local — live HERE under
# .studio/ at the workspace root, OUTSIDE app/agent (the AgentCore codeLocation),
# so no deploy packaging path can bundle them. Never commit .studio/.
.studio/

# `bag dev --container` writes the runtime secret bundle (wallet material +
# unlock password + provider/storage keys) into agentcore/.env.local so the dev
# container can sign. The agentcore/ dir is otherwise committed, so ignore the
# secret file here (never commit it).
agentcore/.env.local

# Grid strategy runtime state: which levels hold lots, and the trade log.
# Machine-specific and rewritten on every trade, so it does not belong in git.
# NOTE the level->lot mapping exists ONLY here — the chain knows the balances but
# not which rung bought them. Losing this file orphans open lots: they stay in
# the wallet but the grid forgets it owns them and will re-buy those rungs.
# Back it up before wiping a host; `python strategy.py grid` prints the mapping.
.grid_state.*.json
.grid_state.*.lock
.grid_state.*.tmp

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.venv-*/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# Editor / OS junk
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# Skills installed at workspace root (CC picks them up automatically;
# they're regeneratable via `bag skills install --scope project`).
.claude/skills/

# Buyer test keystore — local only, never deployed (rsync would otherwise
# carry it to the VPS, which has no business holding the buyer's key).
.studio/wallets-buyer/
